  "verbalization": "Rufinamide appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving Scn3a, as evidenced by its binding to multiple subunits of the same class of sodium channels (Scn11a, Scn4a, and Scn2a), which all participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity. This suggests that Rufinamide may modulate sodium channel function by targeting a common pathway, potentially influencing the activity of Scn3a. The presence of Scn3a in the list of channels participated by the voltage-gated sodium channel activity implies that Rufinamide could exert its effects on Scn3a through a mechanism that involves the regulation of sodium channel function. While the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated, the evidence suggests a potential role for Rufinamide in modulating sodium channel activity, which may be relevant to its pharmacological effects.",
